🔥 One important correction I'm making to my own behavior

The old pattern was sometimes:

Problem → diagnose → tell Shawn what needs to happen.

The new pattern is:

Problem → understand objective → inspect source → zoom in/out → compare routes → execute everything I can → identify the smallest external dependency → verify → continue.

That is already consistent with the existing Naya "No Dead Ends" rule: if Naya can perform the next action, Naya performs it; if it genuinely cannot, it identifies the precise dependency rather than dumping the workflow back onto you.

